{title: 652 - Love at Home}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #652 • LOVE AT HOME • 7.6.8.6}
{lyricist: John H. McNaughton}
{composer: John H. McNaughton}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 652}
{meta: tune LOVE AT HOME}
{meta: meter 7.6.8.6}
{meta: category Christian Home - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]There [F]is beauty [Bb]all around,
[F]When [C]there’s [F]love [Bb]at home;
[F/C]There is [C7]joy [F]in [C]every [F]sound,
[Bb]When there’s [C]love at [F]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Love [Bb]at home, [F/C]love [C7]at home;
[Bb]Time doth softly, [F]sweetly [C]glide,
[F]When there's [Bb]love at [C]home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Kindly [F]heaven smiles above, [Bb]When there's [F]love at home;
[F]All the [C]earth [F]is fill'd with love, When there's [Bb]love at home.
[F/C]Sweeter sings [C7]the brooklet [C]by, Brighter beams the [F]azure sky;
[Bb]O, there's One who smiles [C]on high When there's [F]love at home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Jesus, [F]make me wholly Thine, [Bb]Then there's [F]love at home;
[F]May Thy [C]sacrifice [F]be mine, Then there's [Bb]love at home.
[F/C]Safely [C7]from all [F]harm I'll [C]rest, With no sinful [F]care distress'd,
[Bb]Thro' Thy tender mercy [C]blessed, When there's [F]love at home.
{end_of_verse}
